`find()` claims to return `QueryResult<any>` but the non-array branch can return a non-array in `data` via `data: result.value || result`. If `result` is an object without a `value` array (or already a `QueryResult`-shaped object), this will violate the `QueryResult.data: T[]` contract and can break consumers like `ObjectGrid` that assume `result.data` is an array. Consider mirroring `packages/data-objectstack/src/index.ts` by normalizing to an array (e.g., prefer `result.value` when it’s an array, else fall back to `result.data` when it’s an array, else `[]`) and computing `total` accordingly.
